---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Castalia Programs"
  description="Index institution-ready Castalia courses for licensing, adoption, and resale to universities, schools, and other learning organizations."
  isHomePage={true}
>
  <main class="programs-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero__inner">
        <span class="eyebrow">Institution Sales Index</span>
        <h1>Courses packaged for institutional adoption.</h1>
        <p>
          programs.castalia.institute is the public catalog for Castalia programs offered to
          universities, schools, colleges, accelerators, and workforce partners. It runs on the
          shared @castalia/platform shell so it stays visually and structurally aligned with the
          broader institute web ecosystem.
        </p>
        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/catalog">Browse catalog</a>
          <a class="button button--secondary" href="/institutions">For institutions</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section__intro">
        <h2>What belongs here</h2>
        <p>
          Use this repository to index programs for sale to institutions, not direct-to-learner
          landing pages. Each listing can point to curriculum summaries, deployment notes,
          accreditation context, pricing models, and implementation requirements.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--cards">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Degree-adjacent courses</h3>
          <p>Catalog courses that can be licensed into existing university or school offerings.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Certificate bundles</h3>
          <p>Package related courses as stackable certificates for institutional partners.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Faculty infrastructure</h3>
          <p>Document the platform requirements needed to deploy AI-supported instruction.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section__intro">
        <h2>Repository baseline</h2>
        <p>
          This scaffold includes GitHub Pages deployment, the `programs.castalia.institute` custom
          domain, and the shared Castalia satellite shell. Add new Astro routes under `web/src/pages`
          as the catalog expands.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>GitHub Actions builds the Astro site from `web/` and publishes `web/dist` to Pages.</li>
        <li>`CNAME` is set to `programs.castalia.institute` for GitHub Pages custom-domain support.</li>
        <li>`@castalia/platform` is vendored locally so Pages builds do not depend on sibling repos.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="cta">
      <h2>Ready for first listings</h2>
      <p>
        Add detailed program pages next, then point the domain in DNS to GitHub Pages for this
        repository.
      </p>
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/faq">Review setup details</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
